Imports:
  - Types:
      - RESTResource
      - MCPTool
    From: sententia/endpoints

Usages:
  conventions: .goga/usages/conventions.md
  fastapi: .goga/usages/cooks/fastapi.md
  mcp: .goga/usages/cooks/mcp.md

Annotations: |
  This cell defines a FastAPI application — an HTTP server.
  The cell holds no domain dependencies. Component composition occurs in the root cell.
  The two server modes are mutually exclusive.
  When tools are registered, run() MUST launch MCP Server using Streamable HTTP transport.
  When resources are registered, run() MUST launch FastAPI via uvicorn.

  Apply `conventions` for coding and testing standards.
  Apply the `fastapi` practice for application and route setup.
  Apply the `mcp` practice for MCP Server creation and tool registration.

---

"SententiaApp()":
  location: app.py
  annotations: |
    FastAPI application. HTTP container.
    Accepts REST resources and MCP tools, launches the appropriate server.

    Apply the `fastapi` practice to instantiate the application.
  methods:
    "add_rest_resource(resource: RESTResource) -> void:None": |
      Register a REST resource.

      `resource`: an instance of the mutated `RESTResource` type.
      The URL path derives from the `resource` property.

      Apply the `fastapi` practice to create the route.
    "add_mcp_tool(tool: MCPTool) -> void:None": |
      Register an MCP tool.

      `tool`: an instance of the mutated `MCPTool` type.

      Apply the `mcp` practice to register the tool via decorator.
    "run(host: str = '0.0.0.0', port: int = 8000) -> void:None": |
      Launch the server.

      `host`: bind address. Defaults to "0.0.0.0".
      `port`: server port. Defaults to 8000.

      When tools are registered, launch MCP Server using Streamable HTTP transport.
      Apply the `mcp` practice to configure and start MCP Server.
      Set mcp.settings.host and mcp.settings.port before invoking mcp.run().

      When resources are registered, launch FastAPI via uvicorn.
      Apply the `fastapi` practice to start uvicorn.

